RLK
---

Minimal C99 library for 2D grid-based games and roguelikes.

Build:
  make                  # Build librlk.a
  make lint             # Static analysis (-Werror): lib + test/ + demo/
  make test             # Build + run all tests: unit (test/) + demo harnesses (demo/)
  make demo             # Compile+link the demos (PXL viewer only when PXL_DIR is set)
  make check            # Full validation: lint + test
  make dist             # Vendoring snapshot: rlk-<commit>.tar.gz
  make clean            # Remove build artifacts

Note: the Makefiles use BSD make. On Linux, use `bmake` or `pmake`
instead of GNU make.

Configuration:
  Main configuration is defined in Makefile.inc. Copy config.mk.example to
  config.mk to customize CFLAGS, PXL_DIR or library paths. PXL_DIR is unset
  by default: without it, `make demo` builds only the standalone text demos;
  set it to a pxl checkout (e.g. PXL_DIR = ../../pxl) to also build the PXL
  viewer demo_viewer, with PXL_BACKEND = x11 (default) or sdl.

Vendoring:
  rlk is meant to be vendored as-is: flat sources, no generated files, no
  config header. Build a clean snapshot and drop it into your project:

    bmake dist                          # -> rlk-<commit>.tar.gz
    mkdir -p vendor/rlk
    tar -xzf rlk-<commit>.tar.gz -C vendor/rlk --strip-components=1

  Then either compile the sources directly in your own build system:
    cc -std=c99 -Ivendor/rlk -c vendor/rlk/*.c
  or build the static library with bmake: 'bmake -C vendor/rlk', link with
  -lrlk -lm. Note: Makefile.inc is bmake syntax; with another build system,
  pass -Ivendor/rlk and -ffp-contract=off (determinism contract) yourself.
  Keep LICENSE inside vendor/rlk and record the upstream commit there
  (e.g. in vendor/rlk/VENDORED-AT) so updates stay traceable.
  When vendoring several flat C libraries side by side (rlk and pxl both
  ship err.h/geom.h), use a single include root and prefixed paths:
    cc -Ivendor ...    with #include "rlk/rlk.h"   /* never bare "err.h" */
  Quoted includes inside a header resolve in its own directory first, so
  umbrella headers stay unambiguous regardless of -I order.

Design:
  - Zero allocation: the lib never calls malloc/free; all buffers are
    caller-owned (doc/architecture.md, "Memory model").
  - Determinism: same seed + same build -> identical world, byte for byte
    (build flags enforced in Makefile.inc).

Documentation:
  doc/architecture.md   # Zones (base / domains / user land), memory model,
                        # determinism contract, recipes
  doc/conventions.md    # Naming rules
  doc/metrics.md        # Map quality metrics: what each probe measures, golden
                        # policy, multi-seed report (demo/test_tilemap_gen)

Headers:
  rlk.h                # Umbrella header (includes all of the below)

  Base — core:
    err.h              # Error codes (RLK_OK, RLK_E_INVALID, RLK_E_NOTFOUND)
    hash.h             # Deterministic 64-bit hashing
    fmath.h            # Math helpers (clamp, lerp, smoothstep, distances)
    noise.h            # Noise generation (value, perlin, fbm)

  Base — data (POD, caller-owned):
    entity.h           # Generic entities: fixed-capacity list (push/get/move)
    geom.h             # Rect (region) + lattice (grid geometry on world)
    grid.h             # Coarse float grid with bilinear sampling
    mask.h             # Uint8 mask (weight, density, visibility) + constructors
                       # + 4-connected flood fill / component labelling (rlk_mask_flood, rlk_mask_components)
    poi.h              # Points of Interest (anchor, bbox, type, seed)
    scatter.h          # Stateless jittered-grid scatter (one point per cell)
    tilemap.h          # Tile grid over a world rect + tile props + index/line drawing

  Domain terrain:
    slope.h            # Slope from an elevation grid (Horn 3x3)
    drain.h            # Drainage: fill, D8 flow, accumulation, river SDF
    hydro.h            # Derived hydrology: slope, Strahler order, speed

  Domain nav:
    path.h             # A* pathfinding (integer costs, lattice window) +
                       # rlk_path_snap (nearest enterable cell, ring scan)
    path_distance.h    # Multi-source distance field (flow field, nearest source)

  Domain vision:
    fov.h              # Field of view (recursive shadowcasting)

  Domain worldgen — pipeline (wg):
    wg.h            # Noise-field terrain generation engine
    wg_region.h     # Voronoi region (macro-area) stage
    wg_drain.h      # Drain reading stage
    wg_hydro.h      # Hydro reading stage
    wg_relief.h     # Standardised elevation stage
    wg_rivers.h     # River projection stage
    wg_poi.h        # POI detection stage

  Domain worldgen — structure generators:
    ca.h               # Cellular Automata (caves)
    bsp.h              # Binary Space Partitioning (dungeons)

  Chunked persistent world (on top of the wg pipeline):
    world.h            # rlk_world_t: macro field query without fine generation,
                       # on-demand chunks (seam-coherent), tile diffs applied on
                       # regeneration, save/load (seed + diffs), predicate search

Demos (demo/ is flat like the lib; prefixes mark generic vs demo-only blocks):
  demo/demo_viewer.c         # Generic PXL viewer: demo_viewer [world|ca|bsp] [seed]
                             # (world: stage probes + river/POI/A* path overlays)
  demo/demo_world.c          # Fantasy map in terminal: tilemap_gen + local ca/bsp content per POI
                             # + rlk_scatter_mask points on the forest mask (headless ASCII + stats;
                             # roads/POI networks = game logic, not demoed)
  demo/demo_gis.c            # GIS export: .asc/.pgm rasters for external tools (QGIS/GDAL, terminal);
                             # the same stage/field probes are browsable interactively in demo_viewer
  demo/test_tilemap_gen.c    # Golden map stats per seed, run by `make check` (test_* = harness)
  demo/tilemap_gen.* gen_*   # Fantasy map generator package (pure demo)
  demo/src_*.h               # Viewer demo sources (world/dungeon; pure demo)
  demo/gis_export.h          # Generic GIS export helpers (.asc/.pgm)
  demo/source.h viewer.h viewer_app.h widget.h font_6x10.h
                             # Generic PXL viewer harness (header-only).

